Merge Sort:
Merge Sort uses the divide-and-conquer approach: it divides the array into smaller parts, sorts them, and then merges them.

Case          	Time Complexity
Best Case        	O(n log n)
Average Case	    O(n log n)
Worst Case       	O(n log n)
Space Complexity	O(n)

Merge Sort provides consistent O(n log n) performance.
It requires additional memory for the temporary arrays during merging.
It is suitable for large datasets.
